Description: container-based network emulation framework (SysResEval fork)
 Kathara is a lightweight network emulation system based on Docker
 containers: a lab is a set of machines connected by collision domains,
 deployed and managed through a Python API.
 .
 This package is the fork used by SysResEval, as a plain Python library (the
 Kathara project ships a frozen binary): it adds the switch modes of the
 collision domains (hub, switch, managed switch with VLANs and a console),
 save_lab() / restore_lab() of the machines' filesystems and exec_link().
 The Kubernetes manager works with python3-kubernetes installed.
